# No nested classes

Do not nest a `class` / type definition inside another class.

## Required

1. Move the inner type to its own file (Python: one type per file; C++: own header/TU)
2. Prefer composition / a named collaborator over an inner helper type
3. Nested lambdas / local functions for tiny pure helpers are fine; nested **types** are not

## Why

Nested types hide dependencies, inflate the outer class, and block clean unit testing and DI.
